Palm261_TextAttendant:
	.string "The observation deck upstairs only\n"
	.string "opens at night, when the sky is clear.$"

Palm261_TextGuide:
	.string "Welcome to the STAR PAVILION!\p"
	.string "On still nights, the lake reflects\n"
	.string "every constellation in this hall.$"

Palm261_TextStargazer:
	.string "CHELSIA comes here a lot. She says\n"
	.string "the stars help her think.$"

Palm261_TextKid:
	.string "I found the PIPLUP constellation!\n"
	.string "It's tiny, but it's my favorite!$"

Palm261_TextVisitor:
	.string "When the lake flooded, the staff\n"
	.string "carried every star chart upstairs.$"

Palm261_TextExLantern:
	.string "THE LANTERN\n"
	.string "Four stars around a bright one.\l"
	.string "Sailors on the lake steered by it.$"

Palm261_TextExCrown:
	.string "THE CROWN\n"
	.string "A ring of seven stars that rises in\l"
	.string "spring, over the eastern hills.$"

Palm261_TextExPiplup:
	.string "THE PIPLUP\n"
	.string "A small, faint group of blue stars.\l"
	.string "Easy to miss, hard to forget.$"

Palm261_TextExMirror:
	.string "THE LAKE MIRROR\n"
	.string "A painting of HORIZON's lake at night,\l"
	.string "holding every star of the sky.$"

Palm261_TextExWayfarer:
	.string "THE WAYFARER\n"
	.string "Travelers followed its brightest star\l"
	.string "north, toward the mountains.$"

Palm261_TextExTelescope:
	.string "A model of the pavilion's old\n"
	.string "telescope, made of brass and glass.$"

Palm261_TextExTablet:
	.string "A stone tablet carved by HORIZON's\n"
	.string "first settlers: a map of the sky as\l"
	.string "they saw it, long ago.$"

Palm261_TextExMoonStone:
	.string "A replica of a MOON STONE.\p"
	.string "“Found at the MOON CIRCLE on ROUTE 7,\n"
	.string "where the stars seem closest.”$"

Palm261_TextExTwins:
	.string "THE TWIN LIGHTS\n"
	.string "Two bright stars that cross the\l"
	.string "summer sky together, side by side.$"